setting: a positive number of seconds is a budget: true
setting: empty, zero, negative and unparsable text mean no budget: true
cut: the search completed, cut by its budget: true
cut: its attempts are the full search's first four: true
cut: the full search attempted more: true
cut: the crown is the fastest window it timed: true
cut: the crown is no slower than the untuned default it timed: true
cut: the crowned routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
full: no budget, so the cut crown was not replayed and nothing was cut: true
full: the crowned routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
warm: a budgeted call replays the cut crown, and says it was cut: true
warm: the replayed routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
after: the full search's store replaced the cut crown: true
stores: not every store was refused: true
floor: only the baseline and the untuned default were attempted: true
floor: the full search attempted another candidate before the untuned default: true
floor: the search was cut and ran no beam round: true
floor: the crown is the untuned default's time: true
floor: the crowned routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
